# Lovelace Project

Lovelace is a compiler (written in Ada) for a new Pascal/Ada/Delphi-like language. It emits WebAssembly **components** (`.wasm`) or WAT plus companion WIT. A host embedder can JIT-run those components via the Wasmtime C API.

## Products and link kinds

**`lovelace/`** is the only host **executable**. Every other host crate it uses is a **static** library (`Library_Kind use "static"` in the `.gpr`). Do **not** build `compiler`, `lir`, `common`, `jit`, `tooling`, `hypatia`, `alexandria`, or `format` as shared/dynamic libraries.

The **only dynamic library** in the whole project is Augusta’s native backing (`.so` / `.dll` / `.dylib`) under `augusta/`.

1. **`compiler/`** — static library: compiler (frontend, analysis, codegen).
2. **`jit/`** — static library: JIT runtime; **only** crate that links Wasmtime C.
3. **`lovelace/`** — CLI executable (`lovelace build`, `run`, `doc`, `format`, project/solution/package commands); statically links the host libraries.
4. **`augusta/`** — standard library: `.love` plus optional native Ada (**dynamic** library). One codebase, flavors `native` / `wasi` / `web`.
5. **`tooling/`** — static library: `.pjlove`, `.slnlove`, `.pkglove` files and their behavior. No other crate owns these formats.
6. **`hypatia/`** — static library: **Hypatia** package system (resolve, fetch, local and git dependencies).
7. **`alexandria/`** — static library: parse Lovelace comments/doc-comments and generate documentation.
8. **`format/`** — static library: reformat `.love` to the effective style (`lovelace format`).

Shared Ada: **`common/`**, **`lir/`** — both static libraries.

## Repository layout

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `scripts/` | Compile and run samples |
| `docs/` | Human documentation (CLI, grammar, HOW TOs, feature docs) |
| `compiler/` | Compiler static library |
| `jit/` | JIT static library (Wasmtime) |
| `common/` | Shared host static library |
| `lir/` | LIR static library |
| `lovelace/` | CLI executable |
| `tooling/` | Project / solution / package static library |
| `hypatia/` | Hypatia package manager (static) |
| `alexandria/` | Doc generation static library |
| `format/` | Source formatter static library (`lovelace format`) |
| `augusta/` | Stdlib (`.love` + **the only dynamic** native library) |
| `samples/` | `.love` samples for testing |
| `shared/` | Host GPR switch include only (not a crate; create with the first host crate) |

Build system is **Alire**: **one crate per Ada component**, plus a thin root crate `lovelace_workspace` that only `depends-on` + pins existing crates. See the Alire crates rule. Do not add further top-level **component** crates. Do not put several component GPRs in one `alire.toml`.

## Implement only what is asked

Build piece by piece when instructed. Do not scaffold the whole compiler, invent language syntax, or add crates/files beyond the current task. Create Alire crates only when that component is needed or the user asks.